Fail-Safe Iterator
Q. What is Fail Safe?
- A fail‑safe iterator does not throw an exception if the collection is modified during iteration.
- It works on a clone / snapshot of the collection.

Q. How it works
- Iterates over a separate copy
- Original collection can change without affecting iteration

Example:

ConcurrentHashMap<Integer, String> map = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
map.put(1, "A");
map.put(2, "B");

Iterator<Integer> it = map.keySet().iterator();
while (it.hasNext()) {
    Integer key = it.next();
    map.put(3, "C"); // allowed
}
OR
for (ConcurrentHashMap.Entry<Integer, String> entry: map.entrySet()) {
    map.put(4,"F"); //allowed
}

Common Fail‑safe Collections
- ConcurrentHashMap
- CopyOnWriteArrayList
- CopyOnWriteArraySet
